{"id":"92a5267ae8b8630f","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-martin-axiom-consequences.md","title":"MA Consequences","display":"thm-martin-axiom-consequences — MA Consequences","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-martin-axiom-consequences","aliases":["58-thm-martin-axiom-consequences","MA Consequences","Martin's Axiom Implications"],"display":"thm-martin-axiom-consequences — MA Consequences","depends_on":["[[58-thm-martin-axiom]]","[[58-df-suslin-tree]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-martin-axiom-consequences"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-martin-axiom-consequences</span><span>MA Consequences</span><span>Martin's Axiom Implications</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-martin-axiom-consequences — MA Consequences"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ed2709dc7cd09e87\" href=\"?note=ed2709dc7cd09e87\" title=\"58-thm-martin-axiom\">58-thm-martin-axiom</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"47ecd1e17d0a4400\" href=\"?note=47ecd1e17d0a4400\" title=\"58-df-suslin-tree\">58-df-suslin-tree</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MA}(\\omega_1)\">\\(\\mathrm{MA}(\\omega_1)\\)</span> is the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1\">\\(\\omega_1\\)</span> fragment of Martin's axiom.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R)\\)</span> is the exact ordered-tree predicate.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SH}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SH}_S\\)</span> denotes the Suslin hypothesis, defined below.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}suslin\\text{-}hypothesis\\text{-}definition}\\vdash \\mathrm{SH}_S\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\exists T,R\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}suslin\\text{-}hypothesis\\text{-}definition}\\vdash \\mathrm{SH}_S\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\exists T,R\\in V\\;\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom\\text{-}consequences}\\vdash \\mathrm{MA}(\\omega_1)\\to\\mathrm{SH}_S.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}martin\\text{-}axiom\\text{-}consequences}\\vdash \\mathrm{MA}(\\omega_1)\\to\\mathrm{SH}_S.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Martin-Solovay: consequences of MA.</li>\n<li>The conclusion is stated once: the Suslin hypothesis is exactly nonexistence of an ordered Suslin tree. Further category and measure consequences require their own typed theorem atoms.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-thm-martin-axiom","status":"resolved","id":"ed2709dc7cd09e87","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-thm-martin-axiom]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-suslin-tree","status":"resolved","id":"47ecd1e17d0a4400","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-suslin-tree]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{MA}(\\omega_1)","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega_1","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SuslinTree}(T,R)","di